<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Lain's face, as a single-colour glyph.

    Quick Settings tiles and status-bar icons are alpha masks: Android throws away
    every colour in the drawable and tints the remaining shape to match the system
    theme. Handing it the launcher PNG — which is what "use the app icon" asks for
    literally — produces a solid tinted square, because an opaque photo-like bitmap
    is entirely mask. So this is the app icon in the only form these surfaces can
    render: her silhouette, traced to the launcher art's proportions.

    Long hair framing a rounded head, the fringe's triangular parting at the crown,
    and the two big round lenses cut out with evenOdd so they read as glasses rather
    than as dots. That combination is unmistakably her at 24dp, which a generic
    speech bubble never was.
-->
